Don't write:

E-commerce Website — React + Spring Boot

That sounds like a beginner project.

Instead, your project should eventually be presented more like:

ShopFlow — Distributed Order & Inventory Platform
Built a production-oriented e-commerce platform using Java 21, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, Elasticsearch and React. Implemented concurrency-safe inventory reservation using optimistic locking, idempotent order/payment workflows, Redis caching and rate limiting, Kafka-based asynchronous processing, Elasticsearch product search, JWT/RBAC security, WebSocket order tracking, integration testing with Testcontainers, Dockerized deployment and AWS monitoring.

That's a much stronger interview story.

And the real benefit is that the project forces you to learn the same areas that make Amazon-style OA + backend interviews much easier: DSA, Java, SQL, concurrency, Spring Boot, distributed systems, caching, messaging, and system design.
